Hi Phil,

If I understand correctly, multiplegroups allows one to compare factor scores of the same factors across groups.

My approach is to compare factor scores related to two correlated factors of all observations. In substantive terms, I have 4 items regarding stereotypes against one out-group, and 4 items regarding stereotypes against another out-group. I want to scale all items together, and then find out: which out-group is worse off (by comparing factor scores)? This is why my intuition was to use above model. I am further thinking that if I want my slope parameters to carry all item information, could I not use the model of my first post, and additionally constrain location parameters to all equal 0? Does this approach make sense, or am I off track here?

P.S. Thanks so much for this awesome and quick response!

Tobi

