Sorry, was confused by what out-group meant. I'm somewhat confused by what you are describing since I'm not sure it answers what you want.

If the item models were a Rasch, so all the slopes were fixed and equal, then I'd recommend a Wald test to determine if the sum of the first four intercepts were different from the sum of the last four (and if so, one set would tend to be scored higher than the other). But with only eight items, this would require very large sample sizes to get sufficient power.

Does that help?

Phil

