Yes, in this example it is possible to compare the factor score distributions, but doing things like mean-variance comparisons are not possible since the models will be centered around ~ N(0,Sigma) by definition. This is why I was trying to push for a more model based comparison. If you were somehow able to constrain the intercepts to be equal (not sure how that you be justified....) then freeing the latent means and variances would be possible for comparisons in the model directly. But I'm unsure how exactly you could go about it in a meaningful way.

Sorry if that's not too helpful. Cheers.

Phil

