However I got another doubt; How can I restrict the range of estimated theta. Suppose If I want to constrain it in the range [-4,4].

for e.g.

data(LSAT7)
LSAT7=expand.table(LSAT7)
mod=mirt(LSAT7, 1,itemtype = '3PL')

fscor=fscores(object = mod,method = "WL",response.pattern = c(0,,0,0,0,0),theta_lim = c(-4, 4))

fscor
   Item.1 Item.2 Item.3 Item.4 Item.5        F1    SE_F1

[1,]      0      0      0      0      0 -4.045421 2.001584

###Note:I thought,theta_lim is controlling the range of estimated ability but it is not.

also,
fscor=fscores(object = mod,method = "ML",response.pattern = c(1,NA,NA,NA,NA),theta_lim = c(-4, 4))

> fscor
     Item.1 Item.2 Item.3 Item.4 Item.5  F1 SE_F1

[1,]      1     NA     NA     NA     NA Inf    NA

fscor=fscores(object = mod,method = "ML",response.pattern = c(0,NA,NA,NA,NA),theta_lim = c(-4, 4))

> fscor
     Item.1 Item.2 Item.3 Item.4 Item.5  F1 SE_F1

[1,]      1     NA     NA     NA     NA -Inf    NA

In above cases, I need estimated theta values to be restricted to 4 and -4 respectively. In other words, suppose  actual estimated theta value is 4.5 ( or -4.6) or say Inf like the illustrated case above then the value shown should  the 4 (or -4)

 Is there anyway I can make it happen?

Thanking you,
Irshad

